    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so basically it just feels like the money is just disappearing into nothingness. like i feel like there are extra costs i'm not seeing that are just eating away at my payments. is there something about the way the math is set up that makes it feel like the money is being stolen or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It’s not stolen—it’s just the math of compound interest working against you at the start. Your payment covers the interest that accrued since the last bill *first*, and only the leftover touches the principal, so early on, most of your money feels like it vanishes into fees. Once the balance shrinks enough, that flips, and the same payment starts chipping away noticeably—so you’re not losing money, just front-loading the cost of borrowing.",
      "source": "target",
