      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It feels that way because lenders structure payments to maximize their guaranteed profit first—interest is calculated daily, so any delay or minimum payment means more interest accrues before touching the principal. That’s not a hidden fee, but it’s a system built to favor the lender over the borrower. Your best defense is to make extra principal-only payments whenever possible, or look into income-driven repayment if the terms feel unfair. You’re not crazy—it’s just how amortization is engineered.",
